### Limitations the authors admit
- 2018A&A...617A.120M: Simple chemical model cannot explain inner DCO+ 5-4 emission; single physical profile adopted
- 2017A&A...605A..21C: Inner 50 AU cannot be modeled due to low resolution and dust optical depth
- 2017A&A...605A..21C: Matched-filter fluxes are only lower limits
- 2017A&A...605A..21C: Parameterized models include no chemistry; formation route cannot be distinguished
- 2024ApJ...963..163I: Temperature sample requires three >5σ lines and covers only 26 cores
- 2024ApJ...963..163I: Temperature errors exceed 20 K above 100 K
- 2024ApJ...963..163I: Temperature depends significantly on model and assumed H2 density
- 2024ApJ...963..163I: Pixel RADEX calculations use whole-IRDC average density, column density, and linewidth
- 2024ApJ...963..163I: G014.49 fits are uncertain because of complicated, non-single-Gaussian spectra
- 2024ApJ...963..163I: 300 K pixel temperatures are lower limits and excluded from power-law fitting
- 2024ApJ...963..163I: Larger samples needed for robust correlation conclusions
- 2024ApJ...963..163I: Smoothing dilutes G028.273–00.167 H2CO emission below temperature-measurement requirements
- 2017ApJ...835..174S: Missing flux on scales >4.6'' (1.5 kpc)
- 2017ApJ...835..174S: Only four CO transitions constrain few free parameters; two-phase relies on assumptions
- 2020ApJ...901...62L: Differential missing flux can overestimate line ratios by up to 22% under the adopted assumptions
- 2020ApJ...901...62L: Temperature errors include integrated-intensity fitting errors only
- 2020ApJ...901...62L: Temperature uncertainties exceed 25% above 500 K
- 2020ApJ...901...62L: Viewing geometry provides projected rather than real distances
- 2020ApJ...901...62L: Some para-H2CS tails are shorter than corresponding H2CO tails
- 2020MNRAS.496.5308S: Only 3-4 transitions per sub-region limit modelling reliability.
- 2020MNRAS.496.5308S: Rotational diagrams cannot reliably constrain conditions or distinguish two phases from sub-thermal excitation.
- 2020MNRAS.496.5308S: RADEX temperatures have unconstrained upper bounds.
- 2020MNRAS.496.5308S: 2.73 K background may be inappropriate at the AGN.
- 2020MNRAS.496.5308S: Coarse chemical grid makes tabulated values approximate.
- 2020MNRAS.496.5308S: Sulphur depletion not investigated.
- 2020MNRAS.496.5308S: Cause of Boltzmann/rotational column-density discrepancy remains uncertain.
- 2020MNRAS.496.5308S: CS(6-5) cannot cover the SB ring; CS(3-2) SNR drops outside the ring.
- 2016A&A...590A.127W: 1-D model ignores clumps; collisional rate coefficients incomplete (no H, e-, excited H2), so density and abundance uncertain
- 2016A&A...590A.127W: Clumpy structure in images may not all be real
- 2013Sci...341..630Q: Vertical disk structure is uncertain; vertical N2H+ boundaries fixed
- 2024ApJ...971..176H: alpha_CO depends on the assumed x_CO, which the modeling cannot constrain
- 2024ApJ...971..176H: 13CO 1-0 assumed to share the CO beam filling factor, which may underestimate its excitation temperature
- 2024ApJ...971..176H: Modeling restricted to regions with 13CO 1-0 and 2-1 detections, mostly nuclei and overlap region; cloud-scale average biased low
- 2024ApJ...971..176H: Large uncertainty (factor of about 3) in modeled alpha_CO may smear out trends
- 2015A&A...581A..85P: Resolution too low to fully resolve the disk; edge-on view unfavourable
- 2015A&A...581A..85P: Mass loss rate is a lower limit and uncertain by factor ~3; SO data cannot constrain density and temperature
- 2014A&A...570A..28V: RADEX assumes all transitions sample the same gas, and several ratios use degraded or low-resolution data
- 2014A&A...570A..28V: Chemical modelling is preliminary and compares time-dependent models only at one time step
- 2014A&A...570A..28V: Infrared pumping not considered
- 2018ApJ...861...72C: Data did not initially pass QA2 due to low elevation and array configuration
- 2018ApJ...861...72C: Uniform sphere geometry is a clear limitation; masses are first-order
- 2024ApJ...977...60Q: Disk substructures (rings, gaps) and their temperature effects are not included in the models
- 2024ApJ...977...60Q: Absence of a dip in AS 209 and IM Lup may be due to beam smoothing of small snowlines
- 2024ApJ...977...60Q: Depletion factor explored only on a coarse logarithmic grid
- 2021ApJ...921...97J: CO(3-2) from ATCA is spatially unresolved (5-6'') between W and E and had to be distributed by scaling to CO(6-5).
- 2021ApJ...921...97J: Signal-to-noise is insufficient for lensing reconstruction in E and for p-H2O(2_1,1-2_0,2) in W, requiring adoption of fixed magnification factors from Marrone et al. (2018).
- 2021ApJ...921...97J: [CI](2-1) and p-H2O(2_1,1-2_0,2) are not significantly detected in E, and the lack of [CI](1-0) observations prevents direct measurement of the [CI] excitation temperature and confirmation of the [CI…
- 2021ApJ...921...97J: In the LVG models, T_kin/T_dust is assumed constant across all visual extinctions/densities rather than varying with extinction or density.
- 2021ApJ...921...97J: Observations of important neutral gas coolants [OI] (63 um) and [SiII] (35 um), which contribute >50% of total cooling, are unavailable.
- 2021A&A...652A...5M: Uncertainties in the four-dimensional RADEX parameter space are not straightforward to define
- 2021A&A...652A...5M: RADEX underestimates absorption depths for most E-CH3OH lines
- 2021A&A...652A...5M: Methanol abundance is a rough estimate because H2 column is from 2012 and profile varied
- 2019MNRAS.485.2457H: Coarse spectral resolution (3.4 km/s) may overestimate dispersions and Mach number; Mach number is an upper bound
- 2019MNRAS.485.2457H: Cloud line-of-sight extent unknown; PPV not equivalent to physical space
- 2021A&A...646A..59R: Characteristic emission heights should not be equated with physical disk scale heights; opacity affects interpretation.
- 2021A&A...646A..59R: Continuum, CS and CN vertical profiles are marginally resolved.
- 2021A&A...646A..59R: CO is contaminated by background clouds near ~1.8 and 6–7 km s^-1.
- 2021A&A...646A..59R: Height uncertainties include only formal Gaussian-fit errors.
- 2021A&A...646A..59R: RADEX does not treat line overlaps; modeling is restricted to resolved HF regions.
- 2021A&A...646A..59R: Temperature-density degeneracy and difficult-to-quantify temperature systematics.
- 2021A&A...646A..59R: East-west thermalization differences may not reflect a real physical asymmetry.
- 2021A&A...646A..59R: Very low inferred temperatures pose a gas-phase depletion problem for CN and CS.
- 2021A&A...646A..59R: Higher-resolution, multiple-transition CN observations are needed to confirm cold temperatures and distinct production layers.
- 2026A&A...707A.120H: Did not recover high temperatures (>100 K) at the cloud edge; limited angular resolution and sensitivity
- 2026A&A...707A.120H: Uncertainties exclude systematics from fixed parameters
- 2018Natur.558..260Z: Some lines only marginally detected (~4 sigma)
- 2018Natur.558..260Z: Uncertainty on Cloverleaf amplification not reported
- 2021MNRAS.500.5500B: Large angular distance (~4 deg) to the ALMA TP off position caused spectral ripples that were not removed in post-processing.
- 2021MNRAS.500.5500B: Fainter arcs of the ring are not detected in 13CO J=2-1 due to limited sensitivity.
- 2021MNRAS.500.5500B: ACA is likely missing a fraction of the extended 225 GHz radio continuum flux because its largest angular scale is ~1/3 that of the ATCA 750B configuration at 5.5 GHz.
- 2021MNRAS.500.5500B: Moderate velocity resolution (1.3 km s^-1, sampling the ring across only seven channels) and contamination in the 28.2 and 29.5 km s^-1 channels limit detailed kinematic analysis and cause significan…
- 2021MNRAS.500.5500B: Excitation analysis is restricted to single-dish data (providing only average values affected by beam dilution) due to the lack of interferometric CO J=3-2 observations, and RADEX assumes a homogeneo…
- 2021MNRAS.500.5500B: The molecular ring mass estimate is strongly affected by uncertainties in the X_CO abundance factor, which could be lower in C- and O-deficient LBV nebulae.
- 2021MNRAS.500.5500B: The kinematic duration and average mass-loss rate of the ring are loose limits because the ring width is unresolved (conservatively set to the 7 arcsec ACA beam) and constant expansion velocity with …
- 2024ApJ...977...37N: NH3 and H2CO temperatures cannot be compared quantitatively because of a factor of four beam-size difference and peak offsets
- 2024ApJ...977...37N: 24 micron SFRs are lower limits because masked pixels around bright sources are interpolated
- 2024ApJ...977...37N: Errors on SFR likely underestimated because of IMF stochasticity for small clusters
- 2024ApJ...977...37N: H2CO temperature errors underestimated above 80 K
- 2024ApJ...977...37N: Distances for non-bar clouds may be highly uncertain
- 2024ApJ...977...37N: Single-phase gas assumption is an oversimplification
- 2020ApJ...905..122H: H2 density is not independently constrained by the fits.
- 2020ApJ...905..122H: High optical depths can violate the simple LVG approximation; more rigorous radiative transfer including dust opacity is deferred.
- 2020ApJ...905..122H: State-to-state collision coefficients for CO, C and C+ are unavailable, preventing explicit treatment of these collisions.
- 2020ApJ...905..122H: HD 21997 low-density fits poorly constrain temperature and column density, especially for the blue component.
- 2020ApJ...905..122H: Temperature and filling factor are highly correlated.
- 2020ApJ...905..122H: The faint 49 Ceti C18O line has poorer data quality than the other lines.
- 2020ApJ...905..122H: The available isotopologue resolution does not permit direct radial temperature profiles.
- 2020ApJ...905..122H: Herschel resolution differs substantially, limiting assessment of the C+ contribution.
- 2024A&A...692A.151S: Model is probably not unique; more complex geometries and profiles cannot be dismissed
- 2024A&A...692A.151S: Model fails to reproduce the H30alpha profile asymmetry
- 2024A&A...692A.151S: Continuum SED decomposition is only a rough estimate
- 2024A&A...692A.151S: Distance to M 2-9 is highly uncertain
- 2025ApJ...987..158F: Source companions are unresolved in AS2COS0001.1 and AS2COS0008.1, so [CI] fluxes are likely overestimated
- 2025ApJ...987..158F: Conversion factor constraints are limited to very active sources and need samples across masses and metallicities
- 2025ApJ...987..158F: Absolute CMB effect on individual lines cannot be determined without well-sampled SLEDs and non-LTE modelling
- 2022A&A...667A.131B: Not all sub-regions have been observed at all spatial resolutions for all molecules; NSB-b lacks consistent resolution observations and NSB-c has only a single high-resolution ratio (with HCN(4-3) an…
- 2022A&A...667A.131B: Gas kinetic temperature, gas density (except in E Knot, W Knot, and NSB-a at 40 pc), and linewidth are poorly constrained by the MCMC RADEX fitting across resolutions.
- 2022A&A...667A.131B: Follow-up studies of other nearby galaxies are required to confirm whether HCN(4-3)/HCO+(4-3) and HCN(4-3)/CS(2-1) hold as reliable diagnostics beyond NGC 1068.
- 2024PSJ.....5..221C: Raw statistical significance of the HC15N and H13CN detections is low
- 2024PSJ.....5..221C: HCN and isotopologues were observed on different dates, so variations in Q(H2O) and HCN/H2O enter the uncertainty
- 2024PSJ.....5..221C: CN may have an additional source beyond HCN photolysis, so CN/C15N need not equal HCN/HC15N
- 2015ApJ...814..143A: Smooth spherical shell model does not reproduce fine structure; infrared pumping only partly included
- 2013ApJ...767L..32Y: Synthesized beam highly elongated, so a filling factor of 0.5 was chosen
- 2019ApJ...870L..26C: Ad-hoc use of phase calibrator scans for sky subtraction leaves standing waves and sky lines and high noise
- 2025ApJ...989...83B: Bandpass calibration effects on tau_0 and tau_CO are not quantified
- 2025ApJ...989...83B: CO(3-2) and CO(2-1) opacities are less reliable than CO(1-0), so LTE reconciliation is not attempted
- 2025ApJ...989...83B: Xa1 maximum recoverable scale cannot entirely rule out diffuse emission over larger regions
- 2019MNRAS.483.2014H: Observations cannot constrain sizes of the hot corino and extended envelope
- 2026ApJ..1000..141K: The Band 3 and Band 4 observations were separated by ~9 months (October 2016 to July 2017) without simultaneous millimeter monitoring, though a few percent variability would shift T_CMB by < 0.1 K.
- 2026ApJ..1000..141K: The -6 km/s component cannot constrain f_c due to lack of saturation, leaving its T_ex uncertain.
- 2026ApJ..1000..141K: H13CN and H13CO+ transitions have low S/N (~3), limiting their statistical significance.
- 2020ApJ...894...76W: gamma Vir models lack constraints at other wavelengths; temperature minimum cannot be analyzed
- 2020ApJ...894...76W: Variability at longer timescales cannot be ruled out for gamma Lep
- 2017ApJ...842L..24A: Peak brightness cannot be converted to density without non-LTE excitation modelling, which needs more than one line.
- 2017ApJ...842L..24A: Models are non-rotating and omit chemistry, so SASI signatures cannot be assessed.
- 2024A&A...689A..67G: Single-dish observations lack the spatial resolution to resolve the BCG from the CGM tail, requiring fixed kinematic priors from ALMA and a point-source approximation at 4'' offset to correct for bea…
- 2024A&A...689A..67G: Single-dish detections have low S/N (e.g. S/N = 1.2 for the tail [CI](2-1) component and S/N = 2.4 for BCG CO(7-6)) due to atmospheric absorption at ~595-600 GHz (APEX) and low elevation ~30 deg (NRO…
- 2024A&A...689A..67G: The archival ALMA Band 7 spectrum of 12CO(4-3) for the CGM tail is partially truncated by a spectral window gap around 300-500 km s^-1.
- 2024A&A...689A..67G: Lack of [CI](1-0) and high-J CO (e.g., CO(5-4)) detections for the tail leaves degeneracies in the n_H2-T_kin parameter space and leaves K_vir poorly constrained.
- 2024A&A...689A..67G: The [CI](2-1)-based H2 mass depends strongly on the uncertain Q_21 excitation factor and assumed carbon abundance X_CI.

