  - software: RADEX, ndRADEX
  - parameter: 580 temperatures from 10 to 300 K [Radex modeling: "With the above parameters and the H$_2$CO(3$_{2,1}$–2$_{2,0}$)/H$_2$CO(3$_{0,3}$–2$_{0,2}$) integrated intensity ratio derived from the Gaussian fitting, we then compute the temperatures using a model grid for the H$_2$CO lines encompassing 580 temperatures ranging from 10 to 300 K."]
