  - software: RADEX
  - parameter: n(H2) = 10^5–2.0 × 10^7 cm^-3; N(H2) = 10^22–10^24 cm^-2 [Comparison between LTE temperature and …: "n(H$_2$) = 10$^5$ – 2.0 $\times$ 10$^7$ cm$^{-3}$ and N(H$_2$) = 10$^{22}$ – 10$^{24}$ cm$^{-2}$."]
  - assumption: Density/column-density ranges span continuum-derived core extrema [Comparison between LTE temperature and …: "These ranges come from the minimum and maximum values of the cores derived from the 1.3 mm continuum emission (cite: Sanhueza2019), which include both protostellar cores and prestellar candidates."]
